00:46:41.064 --> 00:46:44.635 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they put in a ban on junk
food advertising to kids

00:46:44.635 --> 00:46:46.637 align:start size:88% position:13%
from six in the morning
till 11 at night.

00:46:46.637 --> 00:46:50.107
They banned all cartoon
characters on kids food.

00:46:50.107 --> 00:46:51.341
So no more Tony the Tiger.

00:46:51.341 --> 00:46:52.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
They killed Toucan Sam
and Tony the Tiger.

00:46:52.676 --> 00:46:55.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Slaughter.
- Yeah they put warning labels

00:46:55.379 --> 00:46:59.082 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the front of packaging
like cigarettes for bad food.

00:46:59.082 --> 00:47:02.186 align:start size:88% position:13%
They limited advertising
of formula to kids.

00:47:02.186 --> 00:47:04.955
They eliminated any
junk food in schools

00:47:04.955 --> 00:47:07.958
and they put in an 18% soda tax.

00:47:07.958 --> 00:47:10.561
And they've funded,
there's been funding

00:47:10.561 --> 00:47:13.130
to assess the impact of this.

00:47:13.130 --> 00:47:14.932
$30 million from
Bloomberg actually

00:47:14.932 --> 00:47:17.668
to fund what this
actually is doing

00:47:17.668 --> 00:47:19.303 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they found
dramatic improvements

00:47:19.303 --> 00:47:21.505
and the most dramatic
benefit wasn't even

00:47:21.505 --> 00:47:22.906
from the soda tax.

00:47:22.906 --> 00:47:26.376 align:start position:0%
It was from the ban on marketing
and the warning labels,

00:47:26.376 --> 00:47:29.780
reduced consumption four
times more than soda taxes.

00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:32.182
- Is the increasing of
taxes on these things,

00:47:32.182 --> 00:47:35.252
is that just really a
short term stop though?

00:47:35.252 --> 00:47:37.521
Because eventually if
you get enough people

00:47:37.521 --> 00:47:39.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
to stop then you don't
have the tax money anymore

00:47:39.022 --> 00:47:41.458
and then you might be funding
other things with tax money.

00:47:41.458 --> 00:47:42.726 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I don't know, I
mean it's been a model

00:47:42.726 --> 00:47:44.228
that you know, is
very controversial

00:47:44.228 --> 00:47:47.497
but the Larry Summers
and Michael Bloomberg

00:47:47.497 --> 00:47:49.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
created a fiscal
taskforce around the world

00:47:49.533 --> 00:47:52.336
of financial, finance
ministers to look at

00:47:52.336 --> 00:47:54.471 align:start position:0%
how do we use financial policies
to change behavior right?

00:47:54.471 --> 00:47:57.174
So you tax the things you
don't want people to do

00:47:57.174 --> 00:47:59.610
and you incentivize the things
you want people to do right?

00:47:59.610 --> 00:48:02.546
So, so savings you
don't tax you know

00:48:02.546 --> 00:48:04.214
and maybe soda you
should tax right?

00:48:04.214 --> 00:48:06.516
And I think that it's been
effective across the world.

00:48:06.516 --> 00:48:08.552 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's just a challenging
thing to do.

00:48:08.552 --> 00:48:10.187
The data is really
clear that it works.

00:48:10.187 --> 00:48:11.688 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yeah.
- Cigarettes,

00:48:11.688 --> 00:48:13.190
we do it on cigarettes.

00:48:13.190 --> 00:48:14.424 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we've done in Berkeley,
we've done it in Philadelphia,

00:48:14.424 --> 00:48:15.893
we've done it in
many, many cities.

00:48:15.893 --> 00:48:17.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the problem is the
food industry fights back.

00:48:17.728 --> 00:48:21.865 align:start size:81% position:19%
So in the last
election, in 2016,

00:48:21.865 --> 00:48:24.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
four cities in California
passed a soda tax.

00:48:24.368 --> 00:48:27.104
There are six cities
totally in the country

00:48:27.104 --> 00:48:29.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the food
industry freaked out.

00:48:29.273 --> 00:48:32.342
So the big soda companies
then created a strategy

00:48:32.342 --> 00:48:34.912
to prohibit future taxes.

00:48:34.912 --> 00:48:36.413
So what they did is for example,

00:48:36.413 --> 00:48:39.850
