two thirds majority

00:48:43.887 --> 00:48:46.423
which would mean it would
cripple local governments

00:48:46.423 --> 00:48:49.259 align:start size:88% position:13%
to fund schools, to
fund police departments,

00:48:49.259 --> 00:48:50.761
fire departments.

00:48:50.761 --> 00:48:53.497
And they didn't care about that

00:48:53.497 --> 00:48:56.566
but they spent $7 million
funding this campaign.

00:48:56.566 --> 00:48:59.403 align:start size:97% position:3%
It would've passed 'cause
people don't like taxes right?

00:48:59.403 --> 00:49:01.538
Five days before the election,

00:49:01.538 --> 00:49:02.773
they went to Governor Brown

00:49:02.773 --> 00:49:04.908
who was also called
Governor Moonbeam,

00:49:04.908 --> 00:49:06.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably the most liberal
Governor in history.

00:49:06.543 --> 00:49:08.645 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Yep.
- They said if you

00:49:08.645 --> 00:49:13.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
don't pass this preemptive
law that prohibits

00:49:13.150 --> 00:49:15.886 align:start size:84% position:16%
future taxes on
soda and junk food,

00:49:15.886 --> 00:49:17.721 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're gonna leave
this ballot measure in

00:49:17.721 --> 00:49:18.889
and you're gonna be screwed.

00:49:18.889 --> 00:49:21.158
So he basically was bullied,

00:49:21.158 --> 00:49:23.393
they made him quote an
offer he couldn't refuse

00:49:23.393 --> 00:49:26.129
like the mafia and he
had to pass this tax

00:49:26.129 --> 00:49:28.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
which now prohibits
future taxes.

00:49:28.365 --> 00:49:30.801 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they're doing this in
state after state after state.

00:49:30.801 --> 00:49:32.736
So all this happens
behind the scenes.

00:49:32.736 --> 00:49:34.771 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's all it.
- Politics is messy.

00:49:34.771 --> 00:49:37.674
- Yeah, and so, so as consumers

00:49:37.674 --> 00:49:39.943
we're sort of like
stuck with you know,

00:49:39.943 --> 00:49:44.948 align:start position:0%
this system that is perpetuating
a disease-creating system

00:49:45.816 --> 00:49:47.217
and a disease-creating economy

00:49:47.217 --> 00:49:51.154 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it's, and it's threatening
our entire way of life

00:49:51.154 --> 00:49:52.389
and people just don't get it.

00:49:52.389 --> 00:49:55.058
It's like if we don't
fix this, you know,

00:49:55.058 --> 00:49:56.960
we're all gonna be
really sick and fat

00:49:56.960 --> 00:49:59.663 align:start position:0%
and get all these chronic
illnesses which we already are.

00:49:59.663 --> 00:50:02.032
Our economy is gonna
be crippled by this.

00:50:02.032 --> 00:50:03.533
I mean think about it.

00:50:03.533 --> 00:50:05.902
If one in two dollars of
our entire federal budget

00:50:05.902 --> 00:50:09.206
is for Medicare, I mean
like there's no money

00:50:09.206 --> 00:50:10.741
for anything else right?

00:50:10.741 --> 00:50:12.943
- Yeah, all right so
we have sick people

00:50:12.943 --> 00:50:15.212
suddenly from all of this
or I guess not so suddenly.

00:50:15.212 --> 00:50:17.014
It's happened over generations.

00:50:17.014 --> 00:50:19.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
We've gotten an economy
that the incentives

00:50:19.549 --> 00:50:20.951
are completely out of whack.

00:50:20.951 --> 00:50:22.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let's talk about that
planet thing too.

00:50:22.819 --> 00:50:24.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
How is this
effecting the planet?

00:50:24.821 --> 00:50:26.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
We've talked a
little bit about it.

00:50:26.523 --> 00:50:27.724
- Yeah, so, so.
- The environment

00:50:27.724 --> 00:50:28.825
and the water.
- We talked about

00:50:28.825 --> 00:50:29.993 align:start size:84% position:16%
some of the
environmental impacts

00:50:29.993 --> 00:50:31.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
but what people
don't realize is that

00:50:31.528 --> 00:50:33.463
the very way we grow food
is threatening our ability

00:50:33.463 --> 00:50:34.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
to grow food because
of its impact

00:50:34.798 --> 00:50:36.500 align:start size:81% position:19%
on our climate
and weather right?

00:50:36.500 --> 00:50:40.303
So, so if you look at end to
end, our entire food system,

00:50:40.303 --> 00:50:42.639
it's 50% of climate change.

00:50:42.639 --> 00:50:44.207
Where fossil fuels
is about a third.

00:50:44.207 --> 00:50:46.843
So it's worse than
fossil fuels, why?

00:50:46.843 --> 00:50:48.345
Deforestation.

00:50:48.345 --> 00:50:50.013
You know we kill seven
billion trees a year,

00:50:50.013 --> 00:50:51.782
the size of Costa Rica.

00:50:51.782 --> 00:50:54.284
Soil erosion from our way
of farming and the killing.

00:50:54.284 --> 00:50:55.952
Factory farming of animals.

00:50:55.952 --> 00:50:57.854 align:start size:84% position:16%
Food waste, transport,
refrigeration,

00:50:57.854 --> 00:51:01.825
all these things end to end,
you add them up and it's 50%.

00:51:01.825 --> 00:51:05.128
The good news is that if
that's true we can fix it.

00:51:05.128 --> 00:51:08.065
And the UN said that if we took

00:51:08.065 --> 00:51:10.367
two million of the
five million degraded

00:51:10.367 --> 00:51:11.835
hectares of land
around the world

00:51:11.835 --> 00:51:14.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
from overgrazing and
from poor farm techniques

00:51:14.805 --> 00:51:16.640 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we convert it to
regenerative agriculture

00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:18.909 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is a way of farming
that restores and builds soil,

00:51:18.909 --> 00:51:21.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
